.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ─── Keel / assistant local state (never commit) ──────────────
.keel-update-check
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.override.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.gemini/.env
.gemini/tmp/

# Keel v5.3.0 — ephemeral session hand-off, regenerated at every close, never in history.
docs/continuation-prompt.md

# ─── Design delivery downloads (staging only) ─────────────────
# The standing path the user downloads a Claude Design export to. The DELIVERY
# is installed at docs/design/design-handoff/ by a wholesale swap (handoff
# contract rule 10) and superseded ones are archived under docs/old/, so both
# are tracked. What lands here is the export around it — the .dc.html
# prototypes, the PackDesk _ds bundle, the design tool's own README — plus a
# second copy of the delivery already tracked once. Auditing it is a Phase 4
# gate step and the findings go in docs/BUILD-SPEC.md §1; the bytes themselves
# are never history. Twice now (DR-001, DR-003) this tree was left behind after
# its audit and dirtied the working tree for weeks.
docs/klytos-cms-redesign/

# ─── The generated static site (build output, never source) ───
# `BuildEngine::buildAll()` writes the published site into the repository root:
# one directory per page plus the shared assets, the SEO surfaces and the x402
# gate. It is OUTPUT — regenerated from `installer/` on every build — and any
# admin save that touches site content triggers it, so it appears in the working
# tree during ordinary development and during every E2E run that exercises a
# save. Committing it would put a build artifact in history and make every
# session's diff depend on which screens its tests happened to save.
#
# `.htaccess` is deliberately NOT listed: it is tracked source that the build
# REWRITES, so it has to stay visible in `git status` — a change there is a real
# change to a file the repository ships.
/home/
/about/
/contact/
/search/
/assets/
/.well-known/
/llms.txt
/llms-full.txt
/robots.txt
/sitemap.xml
/search-index.json
/x402-gate.php
